To save a machine learning model we do always prefer the joblib approch rather then the pickel one because it is more efficiant than it 

IF WE HAVE OUR DATASET IN SIZE OF GBS THEN TO TRAIN A MODEL IS VERY TIME TAKING TO OVERCOME THIS WE ARE GOING TO SAVE THAT MODEL AS FILE A BINARY FILE OR SOMETHING LIKE THAT THIS 
THING IS DONE VIA JOBLIB

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
to save a model

from sklearn.externals import joblib
joblib.dump(reg/clf, "filename.pkl")


to load the model 

reg/clf=joblib.load("filename.pkl")


then we can do --> 

reg.predict([[]]) # can predict data rather than traning model everytime


